Legal says order history may need to be kept 8 years in-country.

446
00:23:28.797 --> 00:23:29.907
Level anchors:

447
00:23:31.257 --> 00:23:34.094
B3: a sound regional deployment design.

448
00:23:34.374 --> 00:23:43.462
B4: sequencing and decision records;. the org model;. cost and risk trade-offs with numbers;. what not to build;. reversible first steps.

449
00:23:44.812 --> 00:23:46.412
What a B4 answer covered:

450
00:23:46.692 --> 00:23:47.801
Framing first.

451
00:23:48.081 --> 00:23:52.177
This is mostly a product-and-org decision with an architecture component.

452
00:23:52.457 --> 00:24:01.396
The candidate named the three hard constraints (residency, payments, cost) and the two-way doors versus the one-way doors (Ch 31).

453
00:24:01.676 --> 00:24:03.340
A country cell, not a fork.

454
00:24:03.620 --> 00:24:08.036
The same code and the same deployment pipeline, running as an in-country cell.

455
00:24:09.386 --> 00:24:15.103
Market configuration (tax, currency, payment adapters, locale) as data and plug-ins.

456
00:24:15.383 --> 00:24:27.757
The global layer is limited to non-personal data: catalog templates, the ML models' training jobs on anonymised aggregates, and engineering tooling (Ch 30, Ch 36).

457
00:24:29.107 --> 00:24:30.280
Cost with numbers.

458
00:24:30.560 --> 00:24:32.843
A minimal HA cell has a fixed floor:

459
00:24:33.123 --> 00:24:37.325
3 AZs, a managed database, Kafka, search and observability.

460
00:24:37.605 --> 00:24:40.635
At 10% of the volume, that floor dominates.

461
00:24:40.915 --> 00:24:52.179
The candidate estimated the cell at ~12% of current spend and named the levers (managed services, smaller search, shared CI) and the risk of passing 15%.

462
00:24:52.459 --> 00:24:53.312
The org.

463
00:24:53.592 --> 00:24:55.661
Platform teams own the cell template.

464
00:24:55.941 --> 00:24:59.909
The two local teams own the market adapters and local operations.

465
00:25:00.189 --> 00:25:03.240
Architecture reviews add a market impact section.

466
00:25:04.590 --> 00:25:08.238
The on-call model covers local hours (Ch 37).

467
00:25:08.518 --> 00:25:09.457
Sequencing.

468
00:25:09.737 --> 00:25:20.318
Make the market configurable inside India first (a reversible step), then stand up a staging cell, run a shadow launch with employees, then a soft launch in one city.

469
00:25:20.598 --> 00:25:23.329
Each stage has a success metric and a rollback.

470
00:25:23.609 --> 00:25:24.569
The curveball.

471
00:25:24.849 --> 00:25:28.497
Retention goes into the cell's archive tier, stored in-country.

472
00:25:28.777 --> 00:25:33.875
The retention policy lives as code per market, and the cost impact is estimated.

473
00:25:34.155 --> 00:25:37.206
The candidate asked legal which fields fall in scope.

474
00:25:38.556 --> 00:25:43.932
The B4 signal: most of the time went on constraints, sequencing, cost and ownership.

475
00:25:44.212 --> 00:25:46.857
