00:31:31.154 --> 00:31:36.146
Design Document (excerpt), Peer Mock Interview Programme for a Study Group of 6.

579
00:31:36.426 --> 00:31:37.322
Status:

580
00:31:37.602 --> 00:31:39.693
Template, Owner: study group lead.

581
00:31:39.973 --> 00:31:44.239
Context, Six engineers targeting senior and staff loops within 8 weeks.

582
00:31:44.519 --> 00:31:48.509
Peer mocks disagree often (L2), and nobody tracks progress.

583
00:31:48.789 --> 00:31:54.186
Decision, Weekly role-swapping mocks using shared interviewer cards and anchored rubrics.

584
00:31:54.466 --> 00:31:59.373
Every session is recorded, and the first two weeks include shadow-scored calibration.

585
00:31:59.653 --> 00:32:01.615
A progress log tracks behaviours.

586
00:32:01.895 --> 00:32:07.549
Related, Ch 57 rubric, Ch 58 anchors, Ch 59 drills.

587
00:32:07.829 --> 00:32:08.789
Requirements.

588
00:32:10.139 --> 00:32:10.971
R1:

589
00:32:11.251 --> 00:32:16.947
Each member does ≥ 2 mocks a week as candidate and 1 to 2 as interviewer.

590
00:32:17.227 --> 00:32:18.059
R2:

591
00:32:18.339 --> 00:32:22.243
Every mock uses a card, a clock and a scorecard with evidence.

592
00:32:22.523 --> 00:32:23.376
R3:

593
00:32:23.656 --> 00:32:30.035
Inter-interviewer verdict agreement ≥ 80% on shared recordings by week 3.

594
00:32:30.315 --> 00:32:31.211
R4:

595
00:32:31.491 --> 00:32:34.840
Each debrief produces two behavioural changes, logged.

596
00:32:35.120 --> 00:32:35.995
R5:

597
00:32:36.275 --> 00:32:41.992
Readiness is declared only after 3 consecutive at-bar mocks with calibrated interviewers.

598
00:32:42.272 --> 00:32:43.680
Decisions in detail.

599
00:32:45.030 --> 00:32:46.054
Card library.

600
00:32:46.334 --> 00:32:54.803
12 prompts, 3 per level, each with hidden requirements, chains and anchors (§2.6, §2.9 as a start).

601
00:32:55.083 --> 00:32:56.150
Calibration.

602
00:32:56.430 --> 00:33:00.014
In weeks 1 to 2, everyone scores the same two recordings.

603
00:33:00.294 --> 00:33:02.897
Discuss the differences, then update the anchors.

604
00:33:03.177 --> 00:33:04.115
Rotation.

605
00:33:04.395 --> 00:33:06.635
Avoid always pairing the same two people.

606
00:33:06.915 --> 00:33:09.411
Rotate prompts so nobody sees one twice.

607
00:33:09.691 --> 00:33:10.694
Claims check.

608
00:33:10.974 --> 00:33:13.001
Every debrief lists the numbers used.

609
00:33:13.281 --> 00:33:16.929
Anyone can run a lab (§5 L3) to verify them.

610
00:33:18.279 --> 00:33:19.004
Log.

611
00:33:19.284 --> 00:33:24.169
A shared sheet with prompt, level, behaviours (yes or no), scores and changes.

612
00:33:24.449 --> 00:33:25.473
Consequences.

613
00:33:25.753 --> 00:33:27.780
About 4 hours per person per week.

614
00:33:28.060 --> 00:33:29.596
Better-calibrated verdicts.

615
00:33:29.876 --> 00:33:34.057
Progress becomes visible through behaviours even while the scores are noisy.

616
